<title>UK: UK trust Angerstein acquires Stace Barr.</title>
<headline>UK trust Angerstein acquires Stace Barr.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK investment trust Angerstein Underwriting said on Monday that it had acquired Stace Barr, a corporate adviser in Lloyd's Insurance market for an initial outlay of 5.5 million stg.</p>
<p>Angerstein said it had already paid 3.5 million stg while the balance would be paid on December 31, 1997.</p>
<p>The firm said it had also completed the acquisitions of Mumford and Coffey.</p>
<p>&quot;Through these three operations, the Angerstein Group now owns, advises or manages 940 million stg in total capacity at Lloyd's representing 9.1 percent of the total market for the 1997 year of account,&quot; Angerstein said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
